<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
DESERT_FAMILY_PORT_EXECUTION_1 (batch SWAC_A, 34 species) - port of
mlie.starwarsanimalcollection into our own defs. Owner ruling 2026-09-20,
verbatim: "All of the desert sheet should be keep but replace with our own
version of creature and art. Port. All of them. Now."

Pattern copied from BMT_FAUNA_ABSORPTION_1
(src/RimStarWars/SWBestiary/Defs/BiomesTeamPort) - reference closure so
nothing dangles (bodies, body parts/groups, eggs, leather/meat/wool/milk
ThingDefs, SoundDefs), donor-framework comps dropped. ONE DEPARTURE from
that precedent: this port does NOT reuse donor textures as final art -
owner asked for "our own version of ... art". Every species has an artpipe
job filed (fill_queue.py, rimflow_item_id DESERT_FAMILY_PORT_EXECUTION_1,
facings south/east/north). Until a render lands, every texPath below still
points at the DONOR'S OWN existing texture file - a LOUD, TEMPORARY
PLACEHOLDER so nothing renders magenta - not final art. Swap texPaths to
our own rendered art path when the artpipe job lands; do not leave this
comment stale once that happens.

Species names are unchanged: every one of these 34 is an attested Star
Wars canon creature (the donor's own flavor text is Wookieepedia-sourced
canon lore) - none needed a NONCANON_BEAST_RENAME_1 draft name.

Wild-biome spawn wiring (race.wildBiomes / the desert-family biome tables)
is deliberately NOT set here - DESERT_FAMILY_PORT_EXECUTION_1 sequencing
step 4 rewires the biome tables last, once all batches land; the precedent
also leaves this field unset in its ported defs.

SWBESTIARY_MISSING_BODYPART_DEFS_1 (2026-09-20): the 8 body-part/group refs
below (SW_Club, SWTailAttackTool, SWHornAttackTool, SW_LeftWing, SW_RightWing,
SW_FrontHorn, SW_LeftHorn, SW_RightHorn) were originally authored with a
stray RSW_ prefix (RSW_Club, RSW_TailAttackTool, ...) that matched no def on
the machine - the sibling RSW_DesertPortA_BodyParts.xml in this same folder
already defines them bare, and SWTailAttackTool/SWHornAttackTool were already
resolving correctly for RSW_DesertPortB_Bodies.xml. Repointed to the existing
bare names rather than adding duplicate RSW_-prefixed defs.
-->
